## Types

```mdl
type EdgeRelease
  desc: |
    One deployed version of one plugin for the `workerd` environment. Immutable once uploaded: a
    second upload of the same key and version is refused unless its hash matches. Stored as a D1 row
    in registry-service beside the plugin's browser `PluginRelease`, with its files in R2 under
    `modules/<slug>/<version>/workerd/`.
  fields:
    pluginKey: NSID              # Config2.Plugin.key, e.g. org.dxos.plugin.markdown
    version: SemVer
    channel: stable | next | dev
    hash: string                 # sha-256 over the WorkerCode the release loads as; the isolate id
    owner: DID | realm:dxos      # who may publish further versions of pluginKey
    manifest: EdgeManifest
    catalog: PluginCatalog
    uploadedAt: Timestamp
    state: pending | uploaded | revoked
```

```mdl
type EdgeManifest
  desc: |
    `Plugin.Manifest` for `dx-env=workerd`, plus what the loader needs to build a `WorkerCode`.
    Module `url`s are names in `files`, not network URLs. Readable without loading any code.
  fields:
    plugin: Config2.Plugin       # key, name, description, icon, dependsOn, ...
    modules: ManifestModule[]    # only modules whose environments include workerd
    mainModule: string           # the generated PluginHost entry
    files: string[]              # every module of the bundle, relative to the release root
    compatibilityDate: Date
    compatibilityFlags: string[]
    bundled: PluginRef[]         # dependsOn plugins compiled into this release, each key@version
    egress?: string[]            # hostnames the plugin fetches; see [F-8]
```

```mdl
type PluginCatalog
  desc: |
    What a release contributes, extracted at build time by activating its modules in a headless host
    (the same activation `activateHeadlessPlugins` runs: Startup, Idle, AssistantStart). Lets the
    registry, the router and MCP answer queries without starting an isolate.
  fields:
    operations: PersistentOperation[]   # key, name, description, inputSchema, outputSchema, services
    skills: SkillRecord[]               # key, name, description, instructions, tools
    types: TypeRecord[]                 # typename, version, JSON Schema of each AppCapabilities.Schema entry
```

```mdl
type OperationRoute
  desc: |
    One row of the operation index: which release implements an operation key on a channel. A key
    belongs to exactly one plugin key; versions of that plugin replace each other's rows.
  fields:
    operationKey: NSID
    pluginKey: NSID
    channel: stable | next | dev
    version: SemVer
    hash: string
```

```mdl
type InvocationScope
  desc: |
    The per-call capability compute-service passes as an RPC argument to `PluginEntrypoint.invoke`.
    Everything that differs between two calls to the same isolate lives here, never in `env`, so one
    isolate serves every space.
  fields:
    spaceId: SpaceId
    caller: Actor
    traceSink: RpcTarget
    cancellation: AbortSignal
    database(): EchoDatabase    # scoped to spaceId; built on DATA_SERVICE and QUEUE_SERVICE
    accessToken(source): string # through the props-bound AccessTokenService
    invoke(key, input): unknown # nested operation, re-enters compute-service
```

## Services

```mdl
service PluginBuilder
  desc: |
    Builds the EDGE release of a plugin from its `dx.config.ts`: evaluates the config with
    `pluginConfigPlugin` for target `workerd`, bundles the module bodies, the bodies of its
    `dependsOn` plugins and a generated `PluginHost` entry into one self-contained module graph (no
    bare `@dxos/*` specifier is left for the runtime to resolve), then activates the result headless
    to write `catalog.json`. `composerPlugin` runs it for external plugins as well.
  ops:
    build(configPath: string, options: { channel, version }) → { manifest: EdgeManifest, catalog: PluginCatalog, files }
  errors:
    BrowserOnlyModule: a workerd module reaches react, react-dom or @dxos/react-ui
    CatalogMismatch: an operation key in the catalog has no handler, or a handler has no key in the catalog
```

```mdl
service PluginStore
  desc: Registry-service storage and query of EDGE releases.
  ops:
    upload(release: EdgeRelease, files) → EdgeRelease
    getManifest(pluginKey: NSID, version?: SemVer, channel?: Channel) → EdgeManifest
    getCatalog(pluginKey: NSID, version?: SemVer, channel?: Channel) → PluginCatalog
    query(filter: { text?, pluginKey?, operationKey?, typename?, skillKey?, channel? }) → EdgeRelease[]
    resolveOperation(operationKey: NSID, channel: Channel) → OperationRoute
    revoke(pluginKey: NSID, version: SemVer) → void
  errors:
    VersionExists: the version is uploaded with a different hash
    KeyConflict: an operation key in the catalog belongs to another plugin key
    NotOwner: the uploader is not the plugin key's owner
```

```mdl
service PluginLoader
  desc: |
    compute-service's Worker Loader client for releases. Uses `LOADER.get` with the release hash as
    the id, so one warm isolate serves every space and every caller of that release, and the
    callback reads R2 only on a cold start. `env` holds only space-agnostic bindings:
    DATA_SERVICE, QUEUE_SERVICE, an AI service and loopback entrypoints from `ctx.exports` whose
    props name the release, never a space. `tails` routes logs to FunctionsLoggerEntrypoint.
  loading: lazy
  ops:
    entrypoint(release: OperationRoute) → PluginEntrypoint
  errors:
    PluginLoadError: the release failed to load or to activate; carries the release and the cause
```

```mdl
service PluginEntrypoint
  desc: The RPC surface `PluginHost` exports from inside the Dynamic Worker, as a WorkerEntrypoint.
  ops:
    describe() → PluginCatalog
    invoke(request: { operationKey, input, pid?, runId? }, scope: InvocationScope) → unknown
  errors:
    OperationNotFound: the release has no handler for the key
```

```mdl
service PluginRouter
  desc: |
    compute-service's resolution of a `dxn:<operation key>[@<version>]` target. It reads the
    operation index (KV snapshot of PluginStore.resolveOperation, refreshed on every upload) and
    falls back to operation-service while operation-service still runs ([F-7]).
  ops:
    route(target: string, channel: Channel) → OperationRoute
  errors:
    OperationNotFound: no release on the channel implements the key
```

```mdl
service PluginSupervisor
  desc: |
    A SQLite Durable Object, one per (space, plugin key), that runs a plugin's durable module as a
    Durable Object facet: `ctx.facets.get(<module id>, () => ({ class:
    worker.getDurableObjectClass(<export>) }))`. The facet owns its own SQLite database; the
    supervisor keeps the release hash, access control and billing counters in its own, which the
    facet cannot read. An upgrade aborts the facet and restarts it with the new release's class;
    its storage survives.
  ops:
    start(spaceId: SpaceId, pluginKey: NSID) → FacetStub
    upgrade(hash: string) → void
    delete() → void
```

## Operations

```mdl
op deployPlugin
  desc: |
    CLI `dx plugin deploy [--channel] [--private]`: runs PluginBuilder, then uploads the release to
    `PUT /registry/edge/plugins/:pluginKey/:version` with a verifiable presentation, API token or
    admin key. A dry-run loads the release in a fresh isolate and compares `describe()` with the
    built catalog before the row is marked uploaded.
  status: unimplemented
  input:
    configPath: string
    channel: stable | next | dev
  output: EdgeRelease
  errors:
    VersionExists: the version is already uploaded with another hash
    KeyConflict: the catalog claims an operation key owned by another plugin
    CatalogMismatch: the loaded release describes a different catalog than the build wrote
```

```mdl
op queryPlugins
  desc: |
    Registry query over EDGE releases, by text, plugin key, operation key, typename or skill key.
    Exposed as `GET /registry/edge/plugins` and as an operation so agents can call it.
  status: unimplemented
  input:
    text?: string
    operationKey?: NSID
    typename?: string
    skillKey?: NSID
    channel?: stable | next | dev
  output: EdgeRelease[]
```

```mdl
op invokeOperation
  desc: |
    The existing `ComputeServiceEntrypoint.invokeOperation`, with `dxn:` targets routed by
    PluginRouter to a PluginEntrypoint instead of to operation-service.
  input:
    key: NSID
    input: unknown
    spaceId: SpaceId
    version?: SemVer
  output: unknown
  errors:
    OperationNotFound: no release implements the key
    PluginLoadError: the release failed to load
  requires: [PluginRouter, PluginLoader]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Deploy a plugin from the CLI
  `dx plugin deploy` builds a plugin's `workerd` release and stores it on EDGE.

  req F-1.1:
    when: a developer runs `dx plugin deploy` in a plugin package
    then: PluginBuilder builds `dx.config.ts` for `workerd`, and the release is uploaded to
          PluginStore as one R2 prefix and one D1 row

  req F-1.2:
    when: a module whose environments include `workerd` reaches react, react-dom or @dxos/react-ui
    then: the build fails with BrowserOnlyModule and nothing is uploaded

  req F-1.3:
    when: a release is uploaded
    then: compute-service loads it in a fresh isolate and compares `describe()` with its catalog; the
          row is marked uploaded only when they match

  req F-1.4: The release is self-contained: its modules import nothing but each other and
    `cloudflare:*`, so a Dynamic Worker can load it from its `modules` map alone.

  req F-1.5: Upload is authorized by the plugin key's owner (DID or realm:dxos); the first upload of
    a key sets its owner.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Versioning
  Releases are immutable and addressed by plugin key, semver and content hash.

  req F-2.1: A (plugin key, version) pair holds one release; uploading it again with another hash
    fails with VersionExists, with the same hash it is a no-op.

  req F-2.2: Every release is on one channel (stable, next or dev); a channel resolves to its newest
    uploaded, unrevoked version.

  req F-2.3: An invocation may name a version (`dxn:<key>@<version>`); without one it runs the
    channel's current version.

  req F-2.4: Revoking a release removes its operation index rows and stops new invocations; the
    previous version on the channel becomes current.

  req F-2.5: The isolate id is the release hash, so a changed release never reuses an isolate of
    the old one and an unchanged release always can.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Types are exposed
  The ECHO types a plugin contributes are visible on EDGE and usable by its operations.

  req F-3.1: A release's catalog lists the JSON Schema of every `AppCapabilities.Schema` entry of its
    workerd modules.

  req F-3.2: PluginHost registers those types in the space registry of every invocation, so a
    handler needs no per-operation `types`.

  req F-3.3: PluginStore.query finds the release that contributes a typename.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Skills are exposed
  The skills a plugin contributes are listed on EDGE and loadable over MCP.

  req F-4.1: A release's catalog lists every `AppCapabilities.SkillDefinition`, with resolved
    instructions and its tool keys.

  req F-4.2: The MCP server's `loadSkill` and the skill list of compute-service's agents read skills
    from the union of current release catalogs.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Operations are exposed and callable
  Every operation a deployed plugin handles can be found and invoked on EDGE.

  req F-5.1: The MCP server's `queryOperations` lists the operations of every current release on
    its channel.

  req F-5.2:
    when: compute-service receives `invokeOperation` for a key a release implements
    then: the operation runs in that release's Dynamic Worker, in the scope of the given space, and
          its result or typed error is returned to the caller

  req F-5.3: A handler's nested `Operation.invoke` re-enters compute-service through a service
    binding, so a call chain across plugins never holds more than one Dynamic Worker per I/O context.

  req F-5.4: An operation key belongs to exactly one plugin key; an upload whose catalog claims a key
    of another plugin fails with KeyConflict.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: compute-service routes invocations to deployed plugins
  compute-service is the single entry for running plugin code on EDGE.

  req F-6.1: PluginRouter resolves a `dxn:` target from the operation index without starting an
    isolate.

  req F-6.2: PluginLoader loads a release with `LOADER.get(hash, ...)`; `env` holds no space id,
    caller or token, and the per-call InvocationScope arrives as an RPC argument.

  req F-6.3: A release that fails to load or activate returns PluginLoadError naming the release; it
    does not affect other releases.

  req F-6.4: Triggers, processes, agents and code-mode scripts invoke plugin operations through the
    same route as `invokeOperation`.

  req F-6.5: Logs and traces of a Dynamic Worker reach the same sinks as other compute-service
    functions, tagged with the plugin key and version.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: operation-service is deprecated and removed
  Plugins stop being compiled into an EDGE worker.

  req F-7.1: While both run, PluginRouter prefers a deployed release and falls back to
    operation-service for keys no release implements.

  req F-7.2: operation-service is removed once every plugin in its static list has a stable release,
    and no caller binds `OPERATION_SERVICE`.

  req F-7.3: The KV operation catalog is rebuilt from release catalogs on every upload or revoke,
    not by a cron that activates plugins.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Durable plugin state through facets
  A plugin module that needs its own storage runs as a Durable Object facet.

  req F-8.1: A module that exports a Durable Object class runs as a facet of a PluginSupervisor, one
    per (space, plugin key), with a SQLite database the supervisor cannot read and the facet cannot
    leave.

  req F-8.2: Upgrading the release aborts the facet and restarts it with the new class; its storage
    is kept.

  req F-8.3: Uninstalling the plugin from a space deletes its facets and their storage.
```

```mdl
feat F-9: Continuous delivery from DXOS
  First-party plugins reach EDGE from the dxos repository without a catalog bump.

  req F-9.1: A merge to `main` deploys every first-party plugin whose release hash changed to the
    `dev` channel, owned by realm:dxos.

  req F-9.2: A dxos release deploys the same releases to `stable`.

  req F-9.3: The workflow runs in dxos CI with an admin credential; edge needs no redeploy.
```

```mdl
feat F-10: Readable manifests and registry query
  Anyone can read what a release contains before running it.

  req F-10.1: `GET /registry/edge/plugins/:key/:version/manifest.json` and `.../catalog.json` return
    the release's EdgeManifest and PluginCatalog as JSON.

  req F-10.2: queryPlugins finds releases by text, plugin key, operation key, typename or skill key.

  req F-10.3: Private releases are returned only to their owner and to members of spaces they are
    shared with.
```

```mdl
feat F-11: Third-party plugins are sandboxed
  A plugin not owned by realm:dxos runs with only the access it declares.

  req F-11.1: A third-party release loads with `globalOutbound` set to an egress entrypoint that
    allows only the hostnames in its manifest's `egress`.

  req F-11.2: Custom CPU and subrequest limits apply to every third-party invocation.

  req F-11.3: InvocationScope grants a third-party plugin only the space of the current call.
```

## Scenarios

```mdl
scenario T-1: Deploy and call a plugin
  given: plugin-markdown at version 0.9.2, an empty dev channel
  when: a developer runs `dx plugin deploy --channel dev`, then MCP invokeOperation calls
        org.dxos.operation.markdown.create in space S
  then:
    - registry-service holds one EdgeRelease for org.dxos.plugin.markdown@0.9.2
    - queryOperations lists org.dxos.operation.markdown.create
    - the document is created in S by the Dynamic Worker, not by operation-service
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: One isolate serves two spaces
  given: a deployed release with hash h
  when: the same operation is invoked in space S1, then in space S2
  then:
    - both calls use the Worker Loader id `plugin:h`
    - each handler sees only its own space's database
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Upgrade a plugin
  given: release 0.9.2 is current on stable
  when: 0.9.3 is deployed to stable
  then:
    - new invocations run 0.9.3 in a new isolate
    - an invocation naming @0.9.2 still runs 0.9.2
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Operation key conflict
  given: org.dxos.plugin.markdown owns org.dxos.operation.markdown.create
  when: another plugin key uploads a catalog that contains the same operation key
  then:
    - the upload fails with KeyConflict
    - the operation index is unchanged
```

## Rollout

1. **Build and store.** `PluginBuilder` emits `workerd` releases; registry-service stores them and
   serves manifests and catalogs ([F-1], [F-2], [F-10]).
2. **Load and route.** compute-service routes `dxn:` targets to releases, with operation-service as
   the fallback; CD deploys first-party plugins to dev ([F-5], [F-6], [F-9]).
3. **Retire operation-service** once every plugin in its list is deployed ([F-7]).
4. **Durable state and third parties** ([F-8], [F-11]).

## Open questions

- **Isolate reuse.** compute-service gives every function invocation a random loader id today, to
  work around WASM memory growth. [F-2.5] needs the reuse that workaround disables; the cause has to
  be fixed or bounded per release.
- **Bundle size.** Each release bundles its own copy of `@dxos/echo`, Effect and the `dependsOn`
  plugins. The size and cold-start cost per release, and any Worker Loader size limit, need
  measuring against operation-service's 3.9 MiB gzip.
- **Concurrency.** A Durable Object may have 10 Dynamic Workers in flight, a Worker request 4. An
  agent process that calls operations of many plugins must spread them across I/O contexts.
- **Version pinning per space.** Whether a space can pin a plugin version, or only the caller.
- **Facet scope.** Whether one supervisor per (space, plugin) is the right grain, or per plugin
  instance object.

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The same plugins that run in Composer run on EDGE. Plugins are deployed from the CLI and stored on EDGE; they are versioned; their types and skills are exposed; their operations are exposed and callable; compute-service executes and routes invocations to deployed plugins; operation-service is deprecated and removed; first-party plugins are delivered continuously from DXOS; and plugin manifests and the registry can be read and queried.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, F-2, F-3, F-4, F-5, F-6, F-7, F-9, F-10]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: EDGE loads plugin code with the Worker Loader API, and potentially with Durable Object facets. The design builds on the `Plugin.config` definition and manifest of dxos/dxos#13893.
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PluginLoader, PluginSupervisor, EdgeManifest]
  source: https://github.com/dxos/dxos/pull/13893
```

```mdl
decision D-3: An EDGE release is the `dx-env=workerd` build of a plugin's `dx.config.ts`, bundled with its `dependsOn` plugins and a generated PluginHost entry into one self-contained module graph. Fills in [D-1] and [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EdgeRelease, EdgeManifest, PluginBuilder, F-1.4]
  why: A Dynamic Worker resolves imports only from its own `modules` map, so a release cannot share `@dxos/*` modules with the host or with other releases; bundling the dependsOn closure lets the plugin activate with the capabilities it requires.
  rejected:
    - One isolate for all plugins, rebuilt on each deploy — it keeps operation-service's coupling, where one plugin's change reloads and can break every other.
    - Ship `@dxos/*` as separate shared modules in each WorkerCode — the bytes are loaded per isolate either way, and version skew between releases becomes possible.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Each release carries a catalog of its operations, skills and types, written at build time by activating the release headless; registry, router and MCP read the catalog and never start an isolate to answer a query. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PluginCatalog, F-3, F-4, F-10, F-1.3]
  why: Readable manifests and registry query need the contributions as data; checking `describe()` against the catalog at upload keeps the two from drifting.
  rejected:
    - Activate releases on a cron to rebuild the catalog, as operation-service does — it costs an isolate per release per minute and fails silently.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Releases are stored by registry-service beside the browser bundle of the same PluginRelease (R2 prefix `workerd/`, one D1 row), are immutable per (key, version), and sit on a channel (stable, next, dev); the uploader of a key's first release owns the key. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EdgeRelease, PluginStore, F-2]
  why: registry-service already owns plugin bundles, versions and private releases; a second store would split one plugin's identity in two.
  rejected:
    - Store releases in compute-service's functions registry — it models single functions with no manifest, types or skills.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The Worker Loader id of a release is its content hash, shared by every space and caller; per-call state (space, caller, trace sink, cancellation) reaches the isolate as an InvocationScope RPC argument, never in `env`. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PluginLoader, InvocationScope, F-2.5, F-6.2]
  why: Worker Loader caches and bills by (id, code); `env` is part of the code, so per-space env would start and bill one isolate per space.
  rejected:
    - A random id per invocation, as functions use today — no warm isolates, and a new billed Dynamic Worker on every call.
    - One id per (release, space) — a cold start and a billed worker per space with no isolation gain, since InvocationScope already scopes data access.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: compute-service resolves `dxn:` operation targets through an operation index that maps each key to exactly one plugin key, falling back to operation-service until it is removed; nested invocations re-enter compute-service through a service binding. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PluginRouter, OperationRoute, F-5.3, F-5.4, F-6, F-7.1]
  why: The index lets routing skip isolate start-up; exclusive key ownership keeps a third-party plugin from shadowing a first-party operation; re-entry keeps each call within the per-I/O-context Dynamic Worker limit.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Durable Object facets host only modules that need their own storage, one PluginSupervisor per (space, plugin key); stateless operations run in a plain WorkerEntrypoint. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [PluginSupervisor, F-8]
  why: Facets add a Durable Object hop and are in beta; operations hold their state in ECHO and need neither.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: First-party plugins are delivered by a dxos CI workflow that deploys changed releases to `dev` on merge to main and to `stable` on a dxos release, as realm:dxos. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9]
  why: The release hash tells CI which plugins changed, so edge needs no catalog bump or redeploy.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Plugins not owned by realm:dxos load with a filtered `globalOutbound` that allows only the hostnames their manifest declares, with custom CPU and subrequest limits. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-29
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [EdgeManifest, F-11]
  why: Deploying from the CLI opens EDGE to code DXOS did not write; egress and limits are the controls Worker Loader offers.
```
